course: dictionary
lesson: 13485
title: Idleness: lazy, or just not in use
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Idleness means not working, and not being busy. Usually it means you are lazy and you do nothing useful. «Tom spent the whole summer in idleness, doing nothing useful at all.» The words «nothing useful» show that idleness is about doing nothing when you could be doing something.
explain: Idleness can also describe a thing that is not being used. «The old printer sat in idleness all weekend, never switched on.» The printer is not lazy, because it is a machine. It is simply not being used, so its idleness means it is sitting still.
explain: In stories and sayings, idleness is often shown as a fault. A wise owl in a fable might say, «Idleness is the root of all mischief», which means that people with nothing to do often get into trouble. Check the context: is someone choosing not to work, or is a thing just not in use?
fact: Idleness is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say «some idleness», not «two idlenesses».
fact: «Idleness» means being lazy and not working or doing anything useful.
fact: «Idleness» can also mean not being in use or not busy, as with a machine.
fact: In old sayings, «idle hands» is used to say that people with nothing to do may get into mischief.
fact: Laziness, or sloth, is an old word for idleness, and in old church teaching it was one of the sins.
exercise: «Tom spent the whole summer in idleness, doing nothing useful at all.» What is idleness? | *Being lazy and not working | Learning new songs | Being kind to animals | Being very fast at sports
exercise: «The old printer sat in idleness all weekend, never switched on.» What does idleness mean here? | Being angry with the printer | Being loud and noisy | *Not being in use or busy | Shining brightly
exercise: In a fable, a wise owl says, «Idleness is the root of all mischief.» What does the owl mean? | *Doing nothing often leads to trouble | Mischief is always a good idea | Working hard makes you tired | Owls like to sleep all day
test: What kind of word is idleness? | *A noun | A place name | A verb
test: Which word is closest in meaning to idleness when it means laziness? | Kindness | Energy | *Laziness | Speed
exam: Which sentence uses idleness to mean a machine is not being used? | Her idleness made her homework late. | *The old machine stood in idleness all winter. | He cooked his dinner with idleness and care.
